  "notes": "{激|はげ}しい is an i-adjective describing extreme intensity, force, or severity.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: {激|はげ}しく (intensely, violently)\n- Noun: {激|はげ}しさ (intensity, severity)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {激|はげ}しい⟦{雨|あめ}→雨：00583_ame⟧: heavy rain\n- {激|はげ}しい⟦{運動|うんどう}→運動：00821_undou⟧: strenuous exercise\n- {激|はげ}しい⟦{競争|きょうそう}→競争：01388_kyousou⟧: fierce competition\n- {激|はげ}しい⟦{痛|いた}み→痛み：01795_itami⟧: severe pain\n- ⟦{気性|きしょう}→気性：10450_kishou⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{激|はげ}しい: to have a violent temper\n\nUSAGE:\nApplies to weather, emotions, physical activity, debates, and personality. Often implies something overwhelming or extreme.\n\nRELATED: ⟦{強|つよ}い→強い：00820_tsuyoi⟧ (strong) is more general; {激|はげ}しい emphasizes violence or extreme force.",
